    <GaugingStation location="Wimpole" name="Rhee" number="33027">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Trapezoidal critical depth flume gauges predominantly Chalk catchment with predominantly agricultural land use and some artificial influences.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Drowns at peak levels; correction incorporated into theoretical rating. Spills occasionally - high flows impeded by bridge abutments 20m d/s. Three peak flow ratings applied across period of record. Part of the Rhee groundwater support scheme.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Trapezoidal critical depth flume, 6.6m broad, horizontal crest 3.8m. Eel tiles installed.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in August 2021 (WINFAP Files v10).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Some surface water and groundwater abstractions in catchment. Runoff increased by effluent returns.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Predominantly Chalk catchment with some Boulder Clay cover in N and W. Land use predominantly agricultural, predominantly arable.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">GEI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Although not gauged to within 30% of QMED, rating accounts for drowned conditions and expected to perform well to QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Few high flow gaugings. Rating can not be validated beyond QMED. Out of bank conditions not considered." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
